00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:25,700
Until our relationship is past the initial viability test?

270
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:27,100
No, problem.

271
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,260
I'm very skilled at postponing intercourse.

272
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,500
I guess I'll call you

273
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:34,300
And we'll arrange another evening.

274
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,560
Yes, I believe protocol dictates that you wait a minimum

275
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,930
Of 18 hours before you call

276
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,760
So I'm not repulsed by your cloying eagerness.

277
00:12:40,830 --> 00:12:41,960
Sure.

278
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:44,230
Again, it's your decision. you're the man.

279
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,630
It wasn't my cat.

280
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,000
It was an experiment

281
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,330
Designed by this guy named schroedinger.

282
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:53,400
From the charlie brown cartoons?

283
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,500
No, he was some kind of scientist.

284
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,130
Let me start again.

285
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,800
Oh, hey, leonard.

286
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,830
Hello.

287
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:00,830
Leslie.

288
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:02,230
Hi.

289
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,900
Okay, well, good night.

290
00:13:10,730 --> 00:13:12,130
Okay, well, good night.

291
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:16,460
That ain't gonna make your point.

292
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:31,500
That's enough.

293
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,900
Call me.

294
00:13:36,930 --> 00:13:38,900
Right.

295
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,360
Okay, good night.

296
00:13:41,430 --> 00:13:42,230
Uh, what?

297
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,000
Had a great time. ciao.

298
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:49,730
I'm sorry, I am not going back to the renaissance fair.

299
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,260
Come on, sheldon.

300
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:55,700
There's so few places I can wear my jester costume.

301
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:58,630
I don't care. there are far too many historical anomalies

302
00:13:58,700 --> 00:13:59,960
For my comfort.

303
00:14:00,030 --> 00:14:01,630
Okay, how about this?

304
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:04,360
You can go dressed as a star trek science officer

305
00:14:04,430 --> 00:14:08,360
Exploring a planet similar to earth in the 1500s.

306
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:10,160
You mean, like spock?

307
00:14:10,230 --> 00:14:11,700
Sure.

308
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:15,200
Fascinating.

309
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:18,200
Hey, fellow scientists...

310
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,860
Sheldon.

311
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:24,430
Why don't we all move over there so leslie can join us?

312
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,760
Yeah, let's do it.

313
00:14:31,230 --> 00:14:33,530
If you're having trouble deciding where to sit,

314
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,300
May I suggest one potato, two potato?

315
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:39,300
Or as I call it, "the leslie winkle experimental methodology."

316
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,400
Don't make this hard for me.

317
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:44,760
It's not hard.

318
00:14:44,830 --> 00:14:46,800
It's simple. you can either sit with me,

319
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:48,330
Your friend, colleague and roommate

320
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,260
Or you can sit with an overrated scientist

321
00:14:50,330 --> 00:14:52,530
You might have sex with.

322
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,560
You're right, it is simple.

323
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,930
Hey, sheldon.

324
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,300
Penny.

325
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:05,630
Third floor tonight-- mixing it up?

326
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,630
I still don't understand why

327
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:11,900
You don't just go to dinner or something.

328
00:15:11,970 --> 00:15:13,200
All right,

329
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,000
Let's say I go to dinner alone,

330
00:15:15,070 --> 00:15:17,330
And during the meal, I have to use the restroom.

331
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:20,670
How do I know someone's not touching my food?

332
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:24,700
Good night, sheldon.

333
00:15:24,770 --> 00:15:28,530
Penny, hold on.

334
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,130
Are you sure things can't work out with you and leonard?

335
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,400
Excuse me?

336
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:36,400
I'm just wondering if you really gave it the old college try.

337
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:40,570
Or in your case, the old community college try.

338
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:44,630
Okay, where is this coming from?

339
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:48,670
Leonard is upstairs right now with my archenemy.

340
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:50,430
Your archenemy?

341
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:53,230
Yes, the dr. doom to my mr. fantastic.

342
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,230
Dr. octopus to my spider-man,

343
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:57,070
The dr. sivana to my captain marvel.

344
00:15:57,130 --> 00:15:58,970
I get it, I get it, I get it.

345
00:15:59,030 --> 00:16:00,870
Do you know, it's amazing how many supervillains

346
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:02,130
Have advanced degrees.

347
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:05,300
Graduate school should probably do a better job

348
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:07,070
Of screening those people out.

349
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:09,100
Sheldon, come back. you're losing me.

350
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,630
It's leslie winkle, penny.

351
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,630
She belittles my research.

352
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:15,000
Oh, sweetie, I'm sorry.

353
00:16:15,070 --> 00:16:17,370
She called me "dumbass."

354
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:19,600
I know. I heard.

355
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:22,130
Given this situation, I have no choice

356
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,970
But to withdraw my previous objections

357
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:27,430
To your ill-considered relationship with leonard.

358
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:30,770
Oh, gee, well, thank you for that.

359
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:32,100
But I think for now,

360
00:16:32,170 --> 00:16:34,000
Leonard and I are just gonna stay friends.

361
00:16:34,070 --> 00:16:36,970
No, that response is unacceptable to me.

362
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:40,470
Sheldon, you are a smart guy.

363
00:16:40,530 --> 00:16:41,740
You must know... I'm "smart"?

364
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:45,290
I'd have to lose 60 iq points to be classified as "smart."

365
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,600
Are you gonna let me talk?

366
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:49,200
I'm sorry.

367
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:52,030
You must know that if leonard and leslie want to be together,

368
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:53,930
Nothing you can do is gonna stop it.

369
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,530
You continue to underestimate my capabilities, madam.

370
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,600
Okay, let me put it this way.

371
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:03,200
If you're really leonard's friend, you will support him

372
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:04,900
No matter who he wants to be with.

373
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:06,670
Wait a minute.

374
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:09,170
Why am I doing all the giving here?

375
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:11,670
If leonard's really my friend,

376
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:13,000
Why doesn't he have to support me

377
00:17:13,070 --> 00:17:14,930
An my hatred of leslie winkle?

378
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:19,300
Because love trumps hate.

379
00:17:19,370 --> 00:17:22,370
Oh, now you're just making stuff up.

380
00:17:22,430 --> 00:17:24,970
Okay, good night, sheldon.

381
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:30,430
Oh, mario, if only I could control everyone

382
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:33,270
The way I control you.

383
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:37,830
Hop, you little plumber, hop, hop, hop.

384
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,890
When the two of you reach a natural stopping point,

385
00:17:43,950 --> 00:17:46,190
I'd like to have a word.

386
00:17:46,250 --> 00:17:49,190
The word is "pee-pee." just do it.

387
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,650
Leonard, you're my friend,

388
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,190
And friends support their friends...

389
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,520
Apparently.

390
00:17:59,590 --> 00:18:04,320
So I'm withdrawing my objection to your desire to have a relationship with leslie.

391
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:06,150
Thank you.

392
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:07,750
I will graciously

393
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:09,390
Overlook the fact that she is an arrogant,

394
00:18:09,450 --> 00:18:12,890
Subpar scientist who actually believes loop quantum gravity

395
00:18:12,950 --> 00:18:15,320
Better unites quantum mechanics with generally relativity

396
00:18:15,390 --> 00:18:16,690
Than does string theory.

397
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,290
You kids have fun.

398
00:18:19,350 --> 00:18:21,450
Hang on a second.

399
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,820
Loop quantum gravity clearly offers more testable predictions

400
00:18:24,890 --> 00:18:26,150
Than string theory.

401
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:29,590
I'm listening. amuse me.

402
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,820
Okay, well, for one thing, we expect quantized space-time

403
00:18:32,890 --> 00:18:34,390
To manifest itself as minute differences

404
00:18:34,450 --> 00:18:36,090
In the speed of light for different colors.

405
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:40,690
Balderdash. matter clearly consists of tiny strings.

406
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:44,690
Are you gonna let him talk to me like that?

407
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:52,320
Okay, well, there is a lot of merit to both theories.

408
00:18:52,390 --> 00:18:53,650
No, there isn't. only loop quantum gravity

409
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,790
Calculates the entropy of black holes.

410
00:18:59,190 --> 00:19:02,150
Sheldon, don't make that noise. it's disrespectful.

411
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:03,250
I should hope so.

412
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,950
It was a snort of derision.

413
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,020
You agree with me, right?

414
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:09,820
Loop quantum gravity is the future of physics.

415
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:15,190
Sorry, leslie, I guess I prefer my space stringy, not loopy.

416
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:16,720
I'm glad I found out the truth about you

417
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:18,590
Before this went any further.

418
00:19:18,650 --> 00:19:20,590
Truth? what truth?

419
00:19:20,650 --> 00:19:22,490
We're talking about untested hypotheses.

420
00:19:22,550 --> 00:19:23,650
It's no big deal.

421
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:25,220
It isn't? really?

422
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:27,720
Tell me, leonard, how will we raise the children?

423
00:19:29,190 --> 00:19:32,620
I... I guess we wait until they're old enough

424
00:19:32,690 --> 00:19:34,990
And let them choose their own theory.

425
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:37,090
We can't let them choose, leonard. they're children!

426
00:19:39,390 --> 00:19:40,720
Wait. where are you going?

427
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:43,450
I'm sorry.

428
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,290
I could have accepted our kids being

429
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,950
Genetically unable to eat ice cream

430
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:49,550
Or ever get a good view of a parade.

431
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,190
But this?

432
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:54,250
This is a deal breaker.

433
00:20:05,690 --> 00:20:11,050
-Look on the bright side. -What's the bright side?

434
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:14,190
Only nine more months to comic-con.

435
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:16,390
Oh, yeah.

436
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:33,430
Captain, I'm getting an unusual reading.

437
00:20:33,490 --> 00:20:34,630
Yeah, that's great.

438
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:35,860
You guys want a corn dog?

439
00:20:35,930 --> 00:20:37,290
Yeah.

440
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,360
That's a temporal anomaly.

441
00:20:39,430 --> 00:20:41,290
Corn dog's didn't come into existence

442
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:43,590
Till the first half of the 20th century.

